& [ClosedForms]
  + RelationshipDirection distinguishes forward from reverse traversal without interpreting prose
  + AnchorRelationshipStep binds relation identity type source target and traversal direction
  + AnchorRelationshipPath binds one seed ordered noncyclic steps and exact candidate target
  + AssociationChannelAccount binds one channel to sorted unique candidate identities and exact contribution count
  + AssociationContribution carries an optional relationship path that is mandatory only for TypedRelation
  + AnchorQueryResult carries canonical relationship_paths and association_account projections

& [Validation]
  + typed relation path length exactly equals RelationHops and every other channel rejects a path
  + the seed begins the first directed endpoint every later step continues from the prior endpoint and the final endpoint equals the candidate unit identity
  + every walked relation identity is retained in contribution evidence and a repeated node refuses as a cycle
  + canonical path derivation sorts and rejects duplicate paths
  + canonical channel accounting groups every candidate contribution without converting or merging channel-local values
  + result validation requires exact equality with both candidate-derived projections
  + result digest commits candidates relationship paths channel account records sources boundaries proof continuation and roots

& [ScannerProjection]
  + typed traversal builds path steps from the admitted SemanticRelation objects already used for direction basis evidence and expansion
  + forward and reverse direction are selected from exact relation endpoints and the current traversal node
  + non-relation scanner stages emit no path
  + final assembly recomputes paths and accounts from the paged candidate set before digest and form validation
  + validate_exact_anchor_scan_result reruns the deterministic scanner against the admitted fabric and detects a relation type or other semantically coherent result mutation that a self-contained form cannot independently adjudicate

& [TestDesign]
